Do you know if Fleet Owners would generally accept this new approach? I am asking because at the moment I do not see any other potential issues except that we make the Fleet owner largely liable for the Driver’s actions etc. Making it possible for drivers to add themselves to a fleet may raise risks for the Fleet Owner, for example driver add themselves to the fleet in bad faith.

Under no circumstances should the Fleet Owner be left without the possibility to remove drivers from their fleet. However would it be possible to also add a step to the flow such as:

# the Driver must first receive a unique identifier from the Fleet Owner;
# Bolt is informed of the unique identifier (or even generates the identifier itself);
# the Driver must then present the unique identifier to Bolt and then they can be added to the correct Fleet

This flow would make it impossible for “random” drivers to ask to be added to any fleet - would this be doable or did you intend to make it possible for any driver to add themselves to any fleet?

