Here’s the {{nodejs-common}} implementation proposal for this feature: [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-nodejs-common/compare/feature/PIF-2112-ct-data-filter-proposal|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-nodejs-common/compare/feature/PIF-2112-ct-data-filter-proposal] 

It adds extra ability to match incoming requests in Router based on the input data. The data is taken from {{options.data_provider}}, which is different depending on the type of router method you’re using. It’s already used for validation, so it was really easy to reuse, and developers will be able to check the interfaces of the autogenerated validators to see what kind of properties they’re supposed to match based on the given router method. For example, for {{router.get("/path", ...)}} we would just match the payload of the query params ({{data_provider}} definition: [link|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-nodejs-common/blob/d0c1a84539b559111f255c84cd835eb9d91effab/src/async/router/authRouter/Router.ts#L640]), while for {{postWithArgs}} we would have to match either {{query}} or {{body}} parameter ({{data_provider}} definition: [link|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-nodejs-common/blob/d0c1a84539b559111f255c84cd835eb9d91effab/src/async/router/authRouter/Router.ts#L806-L808]).

The implementation allows to specify matchers in the {{{[path: string]: string}}} format, for example:

{noformat}{
  "query.city_id": "1",
  "body.order.status": "in_progress"
}{noformat}

As you can see, the filters are string-based to simplify UI handling a bit. Since we don’t want to just show matchers in raw JSON format to the end user, the values that they provide will be strings by default, and I believe that it’s a good compromise between simplicity and functionality.  As for the UI, I suggest to implement matchers as a list of pairs of path+value inputs. It will look similar to the “Endpoints” field(s) for “Request incoming” scope, so there is already a custom field implementation to borrow inspiration from 😉

It would be great to write some unit tests for the matchers (perhaps for the helpers directly, rather than the strategy itself, since we might reuse those helpers in other strategies in the future). It would also be absolutely wonderful to add more comp tests for {{adummy-chaos-testing}} service, since it already setup and tests for {{request_incoming}} scope: [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/32e0e8ea9fddb4980a9a3d95d2a17c106b50573b/src/local/example/adummy_chaos_testing/test/comp/scope/requestIncoming-comp.ts|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/32e0e8ea9fddb4980a9a3d95d2a17c106b50573b/src/local/example/adummy_chaos_testing/test/comp/scope/requestIncoming-comp.ts|smart-link] Finally, once the solution is ready, it would be simply incredible to test it on prelive end-to-end.

